The commission shall have the following duties and functions to:
(1) Annually report to the mayor and aldermen and the chairperson of the board of commissioners of the county on the activities of the commission and, where necessary, to submit recommendations;
(2) Develop, promote, encourage and support activities to achieve a more positive human relations climate in the Milledgeville-Baldwin County community;
(3) Encourage, promote and develop standards for fair and equal treatment and opportunity for all persons regardless of age, handicaps, economic status and type of employment, race, color, creed, sex, religion or national origin;
(4) Coordinate and assist local government to improve human relations in their agencies;
(5) Enlist the cooperation of private industry; community agencies; business, professional, civic and religious organizations; and federal, state, county and municipal agencies in the interest of equal opportunity and treatment of all racial, religious and ethnic groups;
(6) Examine, study and inform the public as to any complaints received concerning discriminatory practices regarding any individual or agency because of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age or handicap; and transmit such complaints to appropriate agencies for investigation and corrective action, when necessary;
(7) Work to remove inequities, which pertain to the status of minority groups in such areas as housing, recreation, education, employment, law enforcement, vocational guidance and related matters;
(8) Provide a forum for airing community problems and grievances, and to promote cross cultural and intercommunity communication;
(9) Stimulate private industry and the business community to create jobs and promote equal employment opportunities; and
(10) Recommend to the board of commissioners of the county and to the mayor and aldermen such additional legislation and programs to effectuate the purposes of this division.
(Code 1986, § 2-129)

